[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:75. SOS]
[00:00.660] Passage 75 | 文章七十五
[00:02.785] SOS | SOS
[00:05.610] When a light passenger plane flew off course sometime ago, | 不久前，一架轻型客机偏离航线时，
[00:11.385] it crashed in the mountains, and its pilot was killed. | 在山区坠毁，飞行员遇难。
[00:16.160] The only passengers, a young woman and her two baby daughters, | 唯一的乘客，一位年轻的妇女和她两个年幼的女儿，
[00:21.340] were unhurt. | 都没有受伤。
[00:23.360] It was the middle of winter. | 当时正值隆冬。
[00:26.125] Snow lay thick on the ground. | 雪厚厚地覆盖着地面。
[00:29.190] The woman knew that the nearest village was miles away. | 这位妇女知道最近的村庄在数英里之外。
[00:33.840] When it grew dark, she turned a suitcase into a bed | 天黑后，她把一个手提箱变成了床，
[00:38.845] and put the children inside it, | 让孩子们睡在里面，
[00:41.120] covering them with all the clothes she could find. | 用她能找到的所有衣服盖住他们。
[00:44.885] During the night, it got terribly cold. | 夜间，天气变得异常寒冷。
[00:49.400] The woman kept as near as she could to the children | 这位妇女尽可能靠近孩子们，
[00:53.025] and even tried to get into the case herself, | 甚至试图自己钻进箱子里，
[00:56.060] but it was too small. | 但它太小了。
[00:58.620] The next morning, she heard planes passing overhead | 第二天早上，她听到飞机从头顶飞过，
[01:03.370] and wondered how she could send a signal. | 疑惑自己如何发出信号。
[01:06.595] Then she had an idea. | 然后她有了一个主意。
[01:09.055] She stamped out the letters SOS in the snow. | 她在雪中踩出了SOS的字样。
[01:14.860] Fortunately, a pilot saw the signal | 幸运的是，一名飞行员看到了信号，
[01:18.525] and sent a message by radio to the nearest town. | 并通过无线电向最近的城镇发送了信息。
[01:22.170] It was not long before a helicopter arrived on the scene | 不久，一架直升机抵达现场，
[01:26.380] to rescue the survivors of the plane crash. | 营救坠机幸存者。